From: SoundTap <noreply@soundtap.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: davinci-mcasp: let a board use AUXCLK without driving AHCLKX

davinci_mcasp_set_sysclk() ties two things together that the hardware keeps
apart: choosing AUXCLK as the high-frequency clock also puts AHCLKX in PDIR, so
the McASP starts driving that pin. For a board that has its own source on the
AHCLKX net, or simply does not route it to the converter, that means the SoC
drives a line it should leave alone.

The Wireless Link is such a board. Its vendor driver, snd-binky.ko, writes
AHCLKXCTL 0x8001 -- AHCLKXE set, so the high clock is internal -- and PDIR
0x14000002, which has the AHCLKX bit clear. Internal clock, pin untouched. That
combination cannot be expressed through set_sysclk(), because every path that
selects AUXCLK also sets the pin bit.

"ti,ahclkx-not-driven" says so in the device tree. It changes nothing for a tree
that does not carry it.

Signed-off-by: SoundTap <noreply@soundtap.invalid>
---
 sound/soc/ti/davinci-mcasp.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/sound/soc/ti/davinci-mcasp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/davinci-mcasp.c
@@ -672,6 +672,7 @@ static int davinci_mcasp_set_sysclk(stru
 				    unsigned int freq, int dir)
 {
 	struct davinci_mcasp *mcasp = snd_soc_dai_get_drvdata(dai);
+	struct device_node *np = mcasp->dev->of_node;

 	pm_runtime_get_sync(mcasp->dev);

@@ -702,6 +703,16 @@ static int davinci_mcasp_set_sysclk(stru
 		set_bit(PIN_BIT_AHCLKX, &mcasp->pdir);
 	}
 	/*
+	 * Selecting AUXCLK above also claimed the AHCLKX pin. A board whose
+	 * AHCLKX net is driven by something else, or is not wired to the
+	 * converter at all, wants the internal clock without that: keep the
+	 * clock and hand the pin back.
+	 */
+	if (np && of_property_read_bool(np, "ti,ahclkx-not-driven")) {
+		clear_bit(PIN_BIT_AHCLKX, &mcasp->pdir);
+		dev_dbg(mcasp->dev, "AHCLKX left undriven by device tree\n");
+	}
+	/*
 	 * When AHCLK X/R is selected to be output it means that the HCLK is
 	 * the same clock - coming via AUXCLK.
 	 */
